{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo"]]},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Silo"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Time Controls"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Limit fetch frequency with throttling, smooth out bursts with debouncing, and keep data current with auto-refresh."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Caching","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/stopAutoRefresh()","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/resumeAutoRefresh()","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/restartAutoRefresh(immediate:)"]},{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Caching","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/ErrorHandling","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Dependencies","doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Prerequisites"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Silo provides three complementary time-based policies. Each addresses a different problem:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Policy"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Problem it solves"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Applied at"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throttle","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prevents too many fetches in a short window"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per fetch call"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Debounce"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Waits for rapid calls to settle before fetching"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Per fetch call","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Auto-refresh","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keeps data current without manual triggers","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Background"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three can be combined with TTL caching — if cached data is still fresh, neither throttle nor auto-refresh will trigger an actual network call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Throttle","text":"Throttle","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throttling enforces a minimum time between fetches. This is the right tool when a fetch can be triggered by rapid user interaction (button taps, scroll-driven prefetching) and you want a hard rate limit regardless of how many calls arrive.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let refreshSource = dataSource {","    try await api.fetchUpdates()","} onError: { _ in .keep }",".throttle(.seconds(2)) \/\/ At most one fetch per 2 seconds",".build()"]},{"anchor":"Drop-vs-Queue-Mode","text":"Drop vs. Queue Mode","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two behaviours are available, selected with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"last","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Drop mode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"last: false"},{"type":"text","text":", the default): the first call in a window fetches immediately. Subsequent calls during the window return the cached value without fetching. The pending calls are silently discarded when the window ends."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".throttle(.seconds(2))         \/\/ First call goes through; others return cache"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Queue mode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"last: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): the first call fetches. Additional calls during the window are deferred. When the window expires, the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"most recent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" queued call is executed."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".throttle(.seconds(2), last: true) \/\/ Last caller always gets fresh data eventually"]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throttling only applies while cached data exists. When the source is empty — for example after the previous fetch failed — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"type":"text","text":" always proceeds to fetch, so a throttled drop can never return the empty value as if it were fetched data."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When to choose:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drop ("},{"code":"last: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Queue ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"last: true"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Manual refresh button","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"✓ First tap always works","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Search-as-you-type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"✓ Last query always resolves","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sensor polling","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"✓ Discard intermediate readings"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Form auto-save","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"✓ Latest input always saves"}]}]]]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Throttle Tolerance","anchor":"Throttle-Tolerance"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Allow the wait timer in queue mode to fire slightly late:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".throttle(.seconds(2), last: true, tolerance: .milliseconds(200))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Debounce","anchor":"Debounce"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Debouncing delays execution until calls have stopped arriving for a specified quiet period. Each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"text":" call resets the timer. Only after the full quiet period elapses does the actual fetch happen.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let searchSource = dataSource { query in","    try await api.search(query: query)","} onError: { _ in .keep }","emptyValue: { [] }",".debounce(.milliseconds(350)) \/\/ Wait 350ms of silence before fetching",".build()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"type":"text","text":" is called three times in 200ms, the first two calls are cancelled and only the third one — after 350ms of silence — triggers a fetch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Tip","style":"tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"250–400ms is a sweet spot for search debouncing. Values under 150ms feel laggy; values over 500ms feel slow."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Debounce-vs-Throttle-Decision-Guide","type":"heading","text":"Debounce vs. Throttle Decision Guide"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Situation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search-as-you-type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Debounce — wait for the user to pause"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refresh button taps"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throttle — first tap always works"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rapid scroll triggers","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throttle — drop intermediate positions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text field auto-complete","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Debounce — only query after typing stops","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pull-to-refresh gesture","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Neither — call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh(clear: true)"},{"text":" directly","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"anchor":"Debounce-and-Cancellation","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Debounce and Cancellation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Callers that are cancelled by a subsequent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"type":"text","text":" call during the debounce window receive a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":". Handle this if needed:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    try await searchSource.refresh()","} catch is CancellationError {","    \/\/ Expected — this call was superseded by a newer one","} catch {","    showError(error)","}"]},{"anchor":"Auto-Refresh","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Auto-Refresh"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Auto-refresh periodically calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"text":" at a fixed interval while the data source has at least one active subscriber to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"valueWithState"},{"text":". When the first subscriber appears, an immediate refresh is triggered before the first interval elapses — so data is never stale on first observation. The timer stops automatically when the last subscriber terminates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let stockSource = dataSource {","    try await api.fetchPrice(ticker: \"AAPL\")","} onError: { _ in .keep }",".autoRefresh(.seconds(10)) \/\/ Poll every 10 seconds while being observed",".build()"]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Timer starts here:","for await price in stockSource.values {","    priceLabel.text = price.formatted(.currency(code: \"USD\"))","} \/\/ Timer stops here (stream ended)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This subscriber-driven design means no background work happens when the UI is off-screen.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Auto-refresh calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"type":"text","text":" internally, so all configured policies still apply — TTL, throttle, and debounce all take effect. If data is fresh within its TTL, an auto-refresh call is a no-op that returns the cached value."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Managing-Auto-Refresh-Manually","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Managing Auto-Refresh Manually"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pause and resume the timer explicitly, for example when the app enters the background:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ AppDelegate \/ SceneDelegate","func sceneDidEnterBackground(_ scene: UIScene) {","    stockSource.stopAutoRefresh()","}","","func sceneWillEnterForeground(_ scene: UIScene) {","    stockSource.resumeAutoRefresh()","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/resumeAutoRefresh()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" resumes the timer and triggers an immediate refresh, ensuring data is not stale for a full interval after the app returns to the foreground."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To reset the interval from zero (and optionally fire an immediate refresh):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Reset the 10-second cycle without an immediate fetch","await stockSource.restartAutoRefresh(immediate: false)","","\/\/ Reset and fetch right now (useful when returning from background)","await stockSource.restartAutoRefresh(immediate: true)"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Auto-Refresh-and-Battery","text":"Auto-Refresh and Battery","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set a tolerance to allow the OS to coalesce wake-ups from multiple timers, reducing CPU wake frequency:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".autoRefresh(.seconds(60), tolerance: .seconds(5))","\/\/ Timer fires between 60 and 65 seconds after each refresh"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For data that refreshes every minute or more, a 5–10% tolerance has negligible UX impact but measurable battery benefit on mobile devices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Combining-All-Three","text":"Combining All Three","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three policies can coexist. Evaluation order within a single "},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["1. TTL check  →  2. Debounce wait  →  3. Throttle check  →  4. Fetch"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If TTL passes (data is fresh), the cached value is returned immediately and the rest of the pipeline is skipped — no debounce wait, no throttle delay, no fetch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A complete example for a live sports scoreboard:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let scoreSource = dataSource {","    try await api.fetchLiveScores()","} onError: { _ in .keep }",".debounce(.milliseconds(100))   \/\/ Absorb rapid-fire triggers from events",".ttl(.seconds(5))               \/\/ Don't re-fetch within 5 seconds",".throttle(.seconds(2))          \/\/ Hard rate limit: max 1 fetch per 2 seconds",".autoRefresh(.seconds(15))      \/\/ Background refresh every 15 seconds",".build()"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/TimeControls"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/silo\/timecontrols"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/Caching":{"role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Prevent redundant network calls by keeping fetched data valid for a configurable duration.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/silo\/caching","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Caching","title":"Caching with TTL","kind":"article"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/ErrorHandling":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/ErrorHandling","title":"Error Handling and Retry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Decide what happens to cached data on failure, and configure automatic retry with backoff strategies."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/errorhandling","kind":"article"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/DataSource/stopAutoRefresh()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Stop auto-refresh timer.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stopAutoRefresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","title":"stopAutoRefresh()","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/datasource\/stopautorefresh()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/stopAutoRefresh()"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/DataSource/resumeAutoRefresh()":{"title":"resumeAutoRefresh()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/datasource\/resumeautorefresh()","abstract":[{"text":"Resume auto-refresh timer.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resumeAutoRefresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/resumeAutoRefresh()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/Dependencies":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Dependencies","title":"Dependencies and Reactive Fetching","abstract":[{"text":"Automatically re-fetch data whenever upstream async stream values change.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/dependencies"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reactive async data management for Swift 6 — fetch, cache, and stream data with zero dependencies."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Silo","url":"\/documentation\/silo","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/DataSource/restartAutoRefresh(immediate:)":{"title":"restartAutoRefresh(immediate:)","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/datasource\/restartautorefresh(immediate:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Restart auto-refresh timer."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"restartAutoRefresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"immediate"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/restartAutoRefresh(immediate:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Silo/documentation/Silo/Prerequisites":{"abstract":[{"text":"Gate fetches on runtime conditions such as network availability or user authentication state.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Prerequisites and Conditional Fetching","url":"\/documentation\/silo\/prerequisites","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/Prerequisites"}}}